; rec45 — EFFECT: ROTARY SPEAKER simulator preset (GUI "Rotary Speaker / Normal Twin, type 0x8A" — name =
; ROM fact via the preset-descriptor table). PM byte-identical to rec30;
; see dsp/sym/rec30.sym for the per-line labels and
; dsp/tremolo-rotary-family.md §4 for the full algorithm (drive ->
; saturation table -> 0.2/0.8 smoother -> crossover [0x8300: drum 500 Hz
; resonator + horn bandpass] -> dual magic-circle rotors with 93 ms rate
; glide [0x830B: drum 5.512 Hz, horn 6.431 Hz, exactly 7:6] -> Doppler
; taps: horn quadrature pair @320+-29, drum antiphase @160+-40).
; This preset's DM voicing: drive 0.1, makeup 3.0, horn BP 1985 Hz r=0.965, horn 0.6, drum 0.485
pm:0x8400  ReadInL                 ; R0 = DM(0x20,I4) — full labels in rec30.sym
pm:0x8416  CallCrossover           ; CALL 0x8300 crossover (drum -> F6, horn BP -> F10)
pm:0x8419  CallRotors              ; CALL 0x830B rate-glide + dual sin/cos rotors
pm:0x841c  HornDelayWrite          ; horn band -> ring @P
pm:0x842f  DrumDelayWrite          ; drum band -> ring @P+520
pm:0x8449  PMStateRewind           ; MODIFY(I8,0x44): 12 state words
dm:0x9806  DrumRotor_Target        ; 0x19BC65 = 5.512 Hz
dm:0x9809  HornRotor_Target        ; 0x1E0676 = 6.431 Hz (7:6)
dm:0xc004  Drive                   ; see header
dm:0xc00c  HornFilt_a1             ; horn bandpass voicing (see header)
dm:0xc01c  HornLevel               ;
dm:0xc01d  DrumLevel               ;
